# Marketing UI

Before writing code here, read `DESIGN.md` (§6 "Marketing Surface") and `PRODUCT.md`.

## Scope

This rule covers the public landing page only: `apps/web/app/page.tsx` and
`apps/web/app/components/landing/**`. The signed-in app (`/app/*`) keeps the
monochrome "Steel and Paper" rules in `DESIGN.md` §2–§5. Never reuse marketing
tokens, the dot grid or glows inside the workspace.

## Copy guardrails

- Positioning: "See what AI tells your buyers about you."
- **Get started** → `/sign-up` (`/app/dashboard` when signed in). **Sign in** → `/sign-in`.
- Pricing: only "Free during beta". No pricing section, no tiers.
- No license name (no MIT) anywhere until a `LICENSE` file exists.
- No Privacy or Terms links until `/privacy` and `/terms` exist.
- No testimonials, customer logos, user counts or benchmarks.
- No weekly/automatic run promises, no absolute privacy guarantees.
- Every illustrative number, answer, brand and competitor is labelled sample data,
  using Acme CRM (brand) and Northwind / Globex (competitors).

## Motion rules

- Scenes animate only while visible (`IntersectionObserver`) and pause when the tab
  is hidden (`visibilitychange`).
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` renders each scene's **final static state** with no animation.
- The pre-JS/SSR frame is the animation's **start** state (empty stage), never the end state.
- Reserve each stage with a fixed aspect ratio per breakpoint; target CLS ≈ 0.
- Animate `transform`, `opacity` and SVG stroke properties only. Ease out with
  `--ease-out-quart` / `--ease-out-expo`. No bounce.
- Hairline icons run once on enter; first and last keyframes are the full icon.
- No video files and no stock footage.

## Components

- Use `Button`/`Sheet`/`Badge` from `@opencited/ui`. Colour, border and variant
  changes belong in `cva` variants in `packages/ui`, not in `className` here.
- Allowed `className` use: layout, spacing, sizing, typography scale, interaction states.
- Internal links use `next/link`. External links (GitHub) use `<a>` with
  `target="_blank"` and `rel="noreferrer"`.
- Keep `page.tsx` a server component. Client components are limited to the animated
  scenes, the mobile menu and any interactive widget.
